  "question": {
    "text": "Monochromatic light of frequency 6.0×10<sup>14</sup> Hz is produced by a laser. The power emitted is 2×10<sup>-3</sup> W. The number of photons emitted, on an average, by the source per second is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>15</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is an integer.&nbsp;Find the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>?&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> W<br /><br />Energy of photon,<br /><br /><math><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></math><br /><br />= 6.6<math><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow></msup></math> J<br /><br />Where <math><mi>h</mi></math> being Planck's constant.<br /><br />Number of photons emitted per second<br /><br /><math><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />= <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>6.6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
